window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-11f142a4ba0aa01a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-and-deploy-internal-apps\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">构建并部署内部应用</h1> <p>使用 Sites 将团队工作流转变为托管式内部应用。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中使用 Sites 构建和测试聚焦的内部应用；在工作流需要时添加存储，并与合适的受众分享经过审核的版本。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>将重复性工作流转化为聚焦型内部工具的团队。</li> <li>需要轻量存储、文件上传或工作区共享的应用。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建并部署内部应用</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 @Sites 为 [describe the workflow or tool you need] 构建一个私有内部应用。请使用任何已附加的文件或链接文档，了解应用面向哪些人、应显示哪些信息，以及人们需要执行哪些操作。\n\n先构建一个范围明确的初始版本，并检查它在手机和桌面设备上是否正常运行。向我展示私有预览，说明哪些内容需要我审核，并让后续迭代变得简单。\n\n未经我事先同意，不要发布或分享此应用、变更其访问权限，也不要联系任何人。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites 文档</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 示例展示（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面的 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"build-and-deploy-from-one-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">在一次任务中完成构建与部署</h2> <p>Sites 是 ChatGPT 中的托管服务。你可以让 ChatGPT 创建应用；它能够构建项目、运行测试、部署应用，并返回一个可供分享的网址。</p> <p>Sites 是否可用取决于你的套餐、功能推出进度和工作区设置。开始之前，请查看 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites#availability-and-usage-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 的可用性和使用限额</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>Sites 的适用范围从静态网站到完整的 JavaScript 或 TypeScript 全栈 Web 应用。因此，它适合构建范围明确的内部工具，例如入职仪表板、培训中心、可搜索的资源库、轻量工作流应用和报告视图。</p> <p>有关设置、存储、部署和访问权限的说明，请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 文档（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>从一个有用的工作流开始。相比要求重建整个内部系统，一个清晰的初始版本更容易审核、部署和改进。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-expect\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">预期效果</h2> <p>下面是一个虚构示例：输入一份附加的发布简报和五个示例请求。第一轮会创建并检查一个范围明确的请求跟踪工具；随后再添加负责人筛选，并让逾期请求更醒目。</p> <p>发布请求跟踪工具打开后会显示 <strong>五个示例请求</strong>，其中包括一个受阻请求、两个审核中请求和一个逾期项目。团队可以按发布计划和状态查看请求、筛选受阻事项、新增请求并更新状态。主要流程和已保存状态都已在桌面与手机屏幕宽度下检查。</p> <p>后续迭代加入了负责人筛选并突出显示逾期事项；<strong>受阻请求仍排在最前面，而且请求没有负责人就不能标记为已就绪</strong>。预览仍为私有状态；没有发布任何 Site，也没有更改访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"give-chatgpt-the-workflow-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">向 ChatGPT 提供工作流背景</h2> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 应用面向谁、用户需要做什么、它应查看哪些来源资料，以及哪些内容需要跨会话保留。明确说明预期的共享范围，并要求 ChatGPT 在部署之前测试主要流程。</p> <p>使用 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（本地尚未收录）</a> 从已连接的内部来源获取或刷新数据。若任务会使用已连接的应用或云端文件，可在网页端的 Work 中启动 Sites 任务，也可在桌面端的 Work 或 Codex 中启动。处理本地文件时使用桌面应用；访问已登录的网站时使用内置浏览器；访问现有 Chrome 会话时使用 Codex Chrome 扩展程序。</p> <p>如果需要实时获取数据，可以通过在 Site 设置中配置的 API 密钥连接第三方工具。不要把密钥等机密值写入提示词或文件。如果要使用插件连接，可以<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-work-from-a-task\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">从当前任务安排工作</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>，让插件按计划获取数据、更新应用，并保存一个供审核的版本。只有获得批准后，才部署审核通过的版本。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-storage-for-the-app\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">为应用选择存储方式</h2> <p>许多内部应用都需要持久化数据。Sites 支持两种存储组件：</p> <ul> <li>对于清单状态、书签、筛选条件、批注、配置和文件元数据等结构化数据，使用 D1（兼容 SQLite 的数据库）。</li> <li>对于已上传文档、图片或其他需要持久保存的文件内容，使用 R2 对象存储。</li> </ul> <p>将结构化元数据存放在 D1 中，将较大的文件对象存放在 R2 中。只读资源页面或小型静态网站可能两者都不需要。</p> <p>存储敏感信息之前，请查看 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites#understand-limits-and-unsupported-uses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 的限制和不支持的用途</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。该指南链接到当前的数据驻留要求，并说明受保护健康信息以及通过第三方处理方进行支付的限制。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-and-share-your-projects\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">管理并分享项目</h2> <p>你可以管理哪些人能够访问已部署的项目。</p> <p>审核内容、数据处理方式和预期受众时，请让新项目保持私有。</p> <p>根据你的账号和工作区设置，你可以与以下对象分享：</p> <ul> <li>你邀请的人。</li> <li>工作区中的所有人。</li> <li>互联网中的任何人。</li> </ul> <p>分享后，其他人可以访问项目，但不能编辑项目。要更改访问权限，请打开 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的 Sites（需联网）</a>，或直接向 ChatGPT 提出请求：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Change this site's access to everyone in my workspace.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">将这个网站的访问权限改为我的工作区中的所有人。</div></div> <p>对于轻量活动指南、俱乐部资源页面或其他面向工作区外人士的网站，也可以启用公开分享。在 Enterprise 工作区中，默认关闭公开发布，必须由管理员启用。即使可以使用公开链接，也应继续保护内部数据的私密性。</p> <p><a id=\"examples\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">示例</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 示例展示（需联网）</a>中包含完整提示词和对应 Site 示例。</p> <ul> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/onboarding-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Onboarding Hub（需联网）</a></strong> 将第一周清单、资源、笔记和上传的文档整合在一起。它使用 D1 保存用户状态和文件元数据，并使用 R2 保存上传的文件内容。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/enablement-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Enablement Hub（需联网）</a></strong> 提供一个可搜索的培训资源库，支持筛选，并用 D1 保存的书签。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/pulse-dashboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pulse Dashboard（需联网）</a></strong> 展示指标、趋势和数据沿袭详情，并使用 D1 保存配置和缓存快照。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/idea-intake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sparkboard（需联网）</a></strong> 将员工创意收集转变为工作流，支持已认证的提交、投票、评论、状态看板和贡献者排名。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/launch-cal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Launch Cal（需联网）</a></strong> 通过月历、筛选条件、风险提示、清单和已连接来源的引用来组织即将发布的产品。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/event-planning-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Event Planning Hub（需联网）</a></strong> 整合活动请求、审批、模板、里程碑、政策准备情况和已连接的规划资源。</li> </ul> <p>可以从这些示例开始，再围绕团队的工作流和来源资料缩小提示词的范围。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-and-deploy-internal-apps\">Build and deploy internal apps</h1> <p>Turn a team workflow into a hosted internal app with Sites.</p> <p>Use Sites in ChatGPT Work to build and test a focused internal app, add storage when the workflow needs it, and share the reviewed version with the right audience.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams turning a recurring workflow into a focused internal tool.</li> <li>Apps that need lightweight storage, uploads, or workspace sharing.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build and deploy an internal app</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Sites to build a private internal app for [describe the workflow or tool you need]. Use any attached files or linked documents to understand who it's for, what information it should show, and what people need to do.\n\nBuild a focused first version and check that it works on mobile and desktop. Show me a private preview, explain anything that needs my review, and make it easy to iterate.\n\nDo not publish or share the app, change its access, or contact anyone without asking me first.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites documentation</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites showcase (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"build-and-deploy-from-one-task\">Build and deploy from one task</h2> <p>Sites is a managed hosting service in ChatGPT. Ask ChatGPT to create an app, and it can build the project, run it for testing, deploy it, and return a URL you can share.</p> <p>Sites availability depends on your plan, rollout, and workspace settings. Check <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites#availability-and-usage-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites availability and usage limits</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> before you start.</p> <p>The scope ranges from static sites to full-stack JavaScript or TypeScript web apps. That makes Sites a good fit for focused internal tools: onboarding dashboards, training hubs, searchable resource libraries, lightweight workflow apps, and reporting views.</p> <p>See the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a> for setup, storage, deployment, and access guidance.</p> <p>Start with one useful workflow. A clear first version is easier to review, deploy, and improve than a broad request to recreate an entire internal system.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-expect\">What to expect</h2> <p>Here is a fictional example using an attached launch brief and five sample requests. The first pass creates and checks a focused request tracker; the follow-up adds an owner filter and makes overdue requests easier to see.</p> <p>The launch-request tracker opens with <strong>five sample requests</strong>, including one blocked request, two in review, and one overdue item. The team can scan by launch and status, filter blocked work, add a request, and update its status. The main flow and saved state were checked at desktop and mobile widths.</p> <p>After a follow-up, the tracker includes an owner filter and highlights overdue work; <strong>blocked requests stay at the top and a request can't be marked ready without an owner</strong>. The preview remains private; no Site was published and access did not change.</p> <h2 id=\"give-chatgpt-the-workflow-context\">Give ChatGPT the workflow context</h2> <p>Tell ChatGPT who the app is for, what people should do, which source material it should inspect, and what should persist between sessions. Be explicit about the intended sharing scope and ask ChatGPT to test the main flow before it deploys.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins (not in this local snapshot)</a> to fetch or refresh data from connected internal sources. Start a Sites task that uses connected apps or cloud files in Work on the web, or in Work or Codex on desktop. Use the desktop app for a local file, the built-in browser for a signed-in site, or the Codex Chrome extension for an existing Chrome session.</p> <p>If you need live data fetching, you can connect to a third-party tool using an API key configured in the Site's settings. Keep secret values out of prompts and files. If you want to use plugin connections, you can <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-work-from-a-task\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule work from the current task</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> to fetch data with plugins on a set schedule, update the app, and save a version for review. Deploy the reviewed version only after approval.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-storage-for-the-app\">Choose storage for the app</h2> <p>Many internal apps need persistence. Sites supports two storage primitives:</p> <ul> <li>Use D1, a SQLite-compatible database, for structured data such as checklist state, bookmarks, filters, annotations, configuration, and file metadata.</li> <li>Use R2 object storage for file bytes such as uploaded documents, images, or other assets that should persist.</li> </ul> <p>Keep structured metadata in D1 and larger file objects in R2. A read-only resource page or small static site may not need either one.</p> <p>Review the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites#understand-limits-and-unsupported-uses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites limits and unsupported uses</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> before storing sensitive information. The guide links to current residency requirements and explains restrictions on protected health information and payments through third-party processors.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-and-share-your-projects\">Manage and share your projects</h2> <p>You can manage who can visit your deployed projects.</p> <p>Keep a new project private while you review its content, data handling, and intended audience.</p> <p>Depending on your account and workspace settings, you can share it with:</p> <ul> <li>People you invite.</li> <li>Everyone in your workspace.</li> <li>Anyone on the Internet.</li> </ul> <p>Sharing lets people visit the project; it doesn't let them edit it. To change access, open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites in ChatGPT (online)</a> or ask ChatGPT directly:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Change this site's access to everyone in my workspace.\n</code></pre> <p>Public sharing also works for a lightweight event guide, club resource page, or other site meant for people outside a workspace. In Enterprise workspaces, public publishing is off by default and an admin must enable it. Keep internal data private even when a public link is available.</p> <h2 id=\"examples\">Examples</h2> <p>The <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites showcase (online)</a> includes Site examples with full prompts.</p> <ul> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/onboarding-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Onboarding Hub (online)</a></strong> combines a first-week checklist, resources, notes, and uploaded documents. It uses D1 for user state and file metadata, and R2 for uploaded file bytes.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/enablement-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Enablement Hub (online)</a></strong> provides a searchable training library with filters and saved bookmarks backed by D1.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/pulse-dashboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pulse Dashboard (online)</a></strong> presents metrics, trends, and lineage details while using D1 for configuration and cached snapshots.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/idea-intake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sparkboard (online)</a></strong> turns employee idea intake into a workflow with authenticated submissions, voting, comments, status boards, and contributor rankings.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/launch-cal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Launch Cal (online)</a></strong> organizes upcoming product launches into a monthly calendar with filters, risk signals, checklists, and connected-source references.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase/event-planning-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Event Planning Hub (online)</a></strong> combines event requests, approvals, templates, milestones, policy readiness, and connected planning resources.</li> </ul> <p>Use those examples as starting points, then narrow the prompt around your team's workflow and source material.</p>"};
